  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Career Quiz Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a career quiz?\", \"a\": \"A career quiz asks about the tasks and settings you enjoy and scores your answers so they point to fields of work worth exploring. The O*NET Interest Profiler, a public example, measures six types of occupational interests. The quiz on this page asks eight questions and names one of six fields.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a career quiz?\", \"a\": \"List the results you want, such as fields of work or your own programs, and describe the quiz in a prompt, including what should happen after each result. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> builds the questions and the database behind them. Publish it and share the link.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I make a free career quiz for my students?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing a career quiz for a class. Describe the grade, the fields of work you want as results, and who should read the answers, then send students the link.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a career quiz for adults ask that a student quiz skips?\", \"a\": \"Ask about work already done: the tasks from past jobs worth keeping, the ones to drop, and the lowest salary the person would accept. Put those after the scored questions so they add context without changing the result. The scoring works like a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/style'>style quiz</a>, where every option points to one result.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions belong in a career quiz for teens?\", \"a\": \"Ask about things a teenager has done: clubs, chores, and weekend jobs. Ask which part of a group project they would take, or whether they would rather fix a bike or design a poster. Keep the wording plain enough to finish on a phone in study hall.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a career path quiz show at the end?\", \"a\": \"It should show the field the answers lean toward, three jobs in that field, and one next step, such as a certificate program or a talk with an advisor. When you build it on Emergent, the app can connect to your course catalog through its API and list those programs on the result screen.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a career aptitude quiz score right and wrong answers?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if you build it that way. Give each question one correct option and map the total score to bands, the same setup as a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/vocabulary'>vocabulary quiz</a>. An interest quiz, like the one on this page, has no wrong answers, because each option points to a result instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"How can I tell whether a free career quiz online is any good?\", \"a\": \"Look at the questions first. Good ones ask about tasks and settings, not job titles. Then look at the result: it should name jobs to explore and a next step, not a personality label. Finally, check that the quiz says who made it and what happens to your answers.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a career quiz help me find work I enjoy?\", \"a\": \"It can narrow the search. A career quiz sorts what you already enjoy into a field of work and names jobs to look into, which gives you a short list to test. Treat the result as a starting point, and talk to someone in one of those jobs before deciding.\"}, {\"q\": \"How can a career coach use a career quiz to find new clients?\", \"a\": \"Put the quiz on a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/free-trial'>free trial landing page</a> next to the offer of a first session at no charge, and send each result by email with a link to book. On Emergent, every taker's answers are saved to a database you own, and responses have no cap.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}